# PocketApp Community Project Rules & Directives

## 1. CODE ARCHITECTURE RULES

### 500-Line Absolute File Size Ceiling
- Every single file created or edited MUST contain **FEWER THAN 500 LINES OF CODE**.
- Never create monolithic files. Decompose components, utilities, and routes into modular files (<500 lines each).
- Top-level components like `App.tsx` must be lean orchestrators (target 40-150 lines, absolute max 500 lines).

### WebContainer & Browser Cross-Origin Isolation
- Caddy / HTTP headers must preserve Cross-Origin Isolation (`window.crossOriginIsolated === true`):
  - `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`
  - `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp`
- Always test with `window.crossOriginIsolated` in mind so WebContainer terminal sessions boot cleanly.

### Community & BYOK Focus
- This repository is the open-source community edition of PocketApp.
- All AI features run on a Bring Your Own Key (BYOK) model with direct provider connections (OpenRouter, Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Groq).
